Z||000000||turbo86se||04-06-2001||10:38 AM||||<BR>This weekend I need to get my SE re-aligned. I had it done once since I got the lowering springs installed, and the steering wheel goes to the left, and the car is a little jumpy on uneven surfaces. I took it back to the place, Gemini, and they couldn't do it b/c of the lip on my 16" wheels. I don't have a set of 14" wheels or anything temporary to put on there except these 185/70/13, but I don't think that would work well. Has anyone had a Fiero laser aligned? Is this better or just as good as a conventional alignment? After reading bhooper's post I'm tempted to take it up to NC to have it aligned. <BR>TIA!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-06-2001||11:06 AM||||I had the same problem. They couldn't attach the mirrors to the wheels. I went to a Goodyear repair shop that had just opened with the new laser alignment machines. It was the best alignment I ever got! They had all they updated specs and the machine printed out a 2-page  report showing all measurements. It took them 4 hours to get it in since I replaced everything but it came out perfect. A few other club members have went there and were very satisfied and how well their alignments came out. Most say it feels better than when it was done by the "mirror machines". Just start calling around. It is most likely in the newer businesses. Like I said mine was at a Goodyear service center.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||turbo86se||04-06-2001||12:51 PM||||music to my ears!<BR>thanks oreif! I hope I don't have any trouble getting up their ramp! That always makes me very nervous.<BR>Thanks again!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||04-06-2001||01:23 PM||||WHen I was in NC I had a helluva time finding a place that would align my 17s. But finally, after flipping out extensively before the Daytona show, I went to a Merchants with a new laser alignment thing- they are in NC, and I don;t know where else, but not here in OH. Anyway they did it, didn't scratch the rims that I could tell and I got a 2 page readout.<BR>||||reg||1
